      "nets": [
        "NET0135",
        "NET0156",
        "NET0098",
        "NET0160"
      ],
      "observed": "The FCC debug connector SWD2 is wired to NET0135 and NET0156 on pins 4 and 6. On the FCC sheet, NET0135 is connected to FCC2 pin 71 (PA15) and NET0156 is connected to FCC2 pin 77 (PB0). The actual SWD pins of the STM32H753, PA13 and PA14, are on FCC2 pins 69 and 70 and carry NET0098 and NET0160, respectively, but those nets do not appear on SWD2.",
      "expected": "The specification states that programming/debug is provided via SWD. For the FCC STM32H753VITx, the SWD header should connect to PA13/SWDIO and PA14/SWCLK, i.e. NET0098 and NET0160, not to PA15/PB0.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "Connections sheet: 'SWD2 Conn_02x05_Odd_Even' with pins '4 NET0135', '6 NET0156', and '10 NET0067'."
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "Flight Control Computer (FCC) sheet: FCC2 pin '69 PA13 NET0098', pin '70 PA14 NET0160', pin '71 PA15 NET0135', pin '77 PB0 NET0156'."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "programming/debug via SWD, USB DFU, and UART-to-USB."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The FCC SWD debug connector is not connected to the MCU's SWDIO/SWCLK pins. Programming or debugging the FCC through the SWD header would fail, and PA15/PB0 are inadvertently exposed on the debug connector.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design contains an anomaly: the FCC SWD debug connector SWD2 is wired to PA15/PB0 instead of the STM32H753's PA13/PA14 SWD pins, breaking the intended SWD programming/debug interface."
}

